{"strongs": "H2320", "word": "חֹ֫דֶשׁ", "translit": "cho.desh", "root": "חדש", "morph": "H:N-M", "pos": "noun masculine", "gloss": "(newness), new moon, month", "definition": "I. חֹ֫דֶשׁ 282 noun masculine Gen 7:11 ( feminine ᵑ0 Gen 38:24 but masculine Sam Di ) (newness), new moon, month (on formation compare Lg BN 144 ; on usage, names, etc., Muss-Arn JBL 1892, 72 ff., 160 ff. ) — ׳ ח absolute Gen 7:11 +; construct (rare) Gen 29:14 +; suffix חָדְשׁוֺ Num 28:14 + 2 t.; חָדְשָׁהּ Hos 2:13 ; Jer 2:24 plural חֳדָשִׁים Gen 38:24 +; construct חָדְשֵׁי Exod 12:2 + 2 t.; suffix חֳדָשָׁיו Job 14:5 + 2 t.; חָדְשֵׁיכֶם Isa 1:14 ; Num 28:11 חָדְשֵׁכֶם Num 10:10 — 1. new moon = day, time, of new moon, as religious festival 1Sam 20:5 ; 1Sam 20:18 ; 1Sam 20:24 ; 1Sam 20:27 ; 1Sam 20:34 ( Dr ); compare ׳ יאֹכְלֵם ח Hos 5:7 a new moon shall devour them , Hi St VB , but on text see We ; usually || שַׁבָּת Amos 8:5 ; 2Kgs 4:23 ; Isa 1:13 (+ קְרֹא מִקְרָא ), מִדֵּי חֹדֶשׁ בְּחָדְשׁוֺ Isa 66:23 , Ezek 46:1 ; Ezek 46:6 (both ׳ יוֺם הַח ), 1Chr 23:31 ; 2Chr 2:3 ; 2Chr 8:13 ; 2Chr 31:3 ; Neh 10:34 (all + מוֺעֵד ), Hos 2:13 ; Ezek 45:17 (both + חג , מועד ); || מוֺעֵד alone Isa 1:14 ; Ezek 3:5 || יוֺם חַגֵּנוּ Ps 81:4 (compare ׳ ראֹשׁ הַח Num 10:10 ; Num 28:11 on religious observance of new moon compare Di Lv p. 578 f Benz Archäol. § 69 ); as time of augury in Babylon (astrological prognostication) Isa 47:13 . 2. month (as beginning with new moon, lunar month; compare Benz Archäol. § 30 , but then, without reference to day of beginning); \\ \\ a. as measure of time during which Gen 38:24 ( J ), Num 11:20 ; Num 11:21 ( J E ), Num 9:22 ( P ), Judg 11:37 ; Judg 11:38 ; Judg 11:39 ; Judg 20:47 ; 1Sam 6:1 ; 1Sam 27:7 ; 2Sam 2:11 ; 2Sam 5:5 ; 2Sam 6:11 ; 2Sam 24:8 ; 2Sam 24:13 = 1Chr 21:12 ; Amos 4:7 ; 1Kgs 4:7 ; 1Kgs 5:7 ; 1Kgs 5:28 (3 t. in verse); 1Kgs 11:16 ; 2Kgs 15:8 ; 2Kgs 23:31 ; 2Kgs 24:8 ; Ezek 39:12 ; Ezek 39:14 ; 1Chr 3:4 ; 1Chr 13:14 ; 2Chr 36:2 ; 2Chr 36:9 ; Esth 2:12 (3 t. in verse). In 1Sam 10:27 b read probably כְּמֵחֹדֶשׁ for ᵑ0 כמחרישׁ , and join to 1Sam 11:1 , so ᵐ5 We Dr (compare Gen 38:24 ); in combinations, יָמִים ׳ ח a month (of) time (compare יֶרַח ימים Deut 21:1 ; 2Kgs 15:13 ) Gen 29:14 ( J ), Num 11:20 ; Num 11:26 ( J E ), ׳ ימים ארבעה ח Judg 19:2 of age ׳ מִסְפַּרחֿ number of his months =length of his life Job 14:5 ; Job 21:21 compare especially ׳ בֶּןחֿ Lev 27:6 ; Num 3:15 ; Num 3:22 ; Num 3:28 ; Num 3:34 ; Num 3:39 ; Num 3:40 ; Num 3:43 ; Num 18:16 ; Num 26:22 (all P ). \\ \\ b. calendar months , (1) with names הָאָבִיב ׳ ח Exod 13:4 ; Exod 23:15 ; Exod 34:18 (twice in verse) (all J E ; = 1st month Exod 12:2 P ), Deut 16:11 זִו ׳ ח 1Kgs 6:1 ( = 2nd mo. ib.; = יֶרַח זִו v 1Kgs 6:37 ); compare 1Kgs 8:2 ( הַשְּׁבִיעִי ׳ הַח = יֶרַךְ הָאֵתָנִים ), 1Kgs 6:38 ( הַשְּׁמִינִי ׳ הַח = יֶרַח בּוּל ); in the post-exilic books occur Babylonian names (see the several words): — נִיסָן ׳ ח Neh 2:1 ; Esth 3:7 ( = 1st mo. Esth 3:7 ); סִיוָן ׳ ח Esth 8:9 = 3rd mo.; כִּסְלֵו ׳ ח Zech 7:1 ; Neh 1:1 ( = 9th mo. Zech 7:1 ); טֵבֵ֑ת ׳ ח Esth 2:16 = 10th mo.; שְׁבָט ׳ ח Zech 1:7 = 11th mo.; אֲדָר ׳ ח Esth 3:7 ; Esth 3:13 ; Esth 8:12 ; Esth 9:1 in all = 12th mo., Esth 9:15 ; Esth 9:17 ; Esth 9:19 ; Esth 9:21 (compare also אֱלוּל Neh 6:15 , without ׳ ח or יֶרַךְ ; this was 6th mo.; see further Schr COT Neh 1:1 Benz l.c .). (2) merely numbered (chiefly P and late) e.g. הַשֵּׁנִי ׳ בַּח Gen 7:11 , compare Gen 8:4 ; Gen 8:5 ; Gen 8:14 ; Lev 16:29 ; Num 1:1 ; Num 1:18 (all P ) + often P ; Deut 1:3 ( P ), 1Kgs 12:32 ; 1Kgs 12:33 ; 1Kgs 25:1 ; 1Kgs 25:3 ; 1Kgs 25:8 ; 1Kgs 25:25 ; 1Kgs 25:27 ; + 11 t. Jeremiah; Ezek 24:1 ; Ezek 32:1 ; Hag 1:1 ; Hag 1:15 ; Zech 1:1 ; Zech 7:1 ; Zech 7:13 ; 1Chr 12:15 , compare entire list 1Chr 27:2-15 ; 2Chr 3:2 + 12 t. 2 Chronicles; Ezra 3:1 + 10 t. Ezra; Neh 7:72 ; Neh 8:2 ; Neh 8:14 ; Esth 3:12 note especially הַזֶּה לָכֶם ראֹשׁ חָדָשִׁ֑ים רִאשׁוֺן הוּא לָכֶם ׳ הַח Exod 12:2 ( P ), as implying that the 1st mo. was formerly not in the spring; observe also usage of omitting ׳ ח , e.g. בָּרִאשׁוֺן = ׳ הָר ׳ בַּח Gen 8:13 , compare v Gen 8:5 so commonly in Ezek.: — Ezek 1:1 ; Ezek 8:1 ; Ezek 20:1 ; Ezek 29:1 ; Ezek 29:17 ; Ezek 30:20 ; Ezek 31:1 ; Ezek 33:21 ; Ezek 45:18 ; Ezek 45:21 ; Ezek 45:25 + Ezek 26:1 ; Ezek 32:17 ; Ezek 45:20 Co ; ( ׳ ח sometimes expressed, see Ezek 24:1 ; Ezek 32:1 above; on like usage with יום see יום ). (3) special phrases and usages are: — עֹלַת חֹדֶשׁ בְּחָדְשׁוֺ לְחָדְשֵׁי שָׁנָה Num 28:14 ( P ; compare יום , and Isa 66:23 above 1. ); מִיּוֺם לְיוֺם וּמֵחֹדֶשׁ לְחֹדֶשׁ Esth 3:7 from day to day and from month to month ; חָדְשָׁהּ Jer 2:24 of wild she-ass's mating time.", "definition_html": "<h1><entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB2579')\">BDB2579</entry> [<entry onclick=\"sn('H2320')\">H2320</entry>]</h1><div class=\"navigation\"><entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB2578')\">BDB2578</entry> | BIBLICAL HEBREW | <entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB2580')\">BDB2580</entry></div><p> I. <bdbheb>חֹ֫דֶשׁ</bdbheb><sub>282</sub> <b>noun masculine</b><sup><ref ref=\"Gen 7:11\" b=\"1\" cBegin=\"7\" vBegin=\"11\" cEnd=\"7\" vEnd=\"11\" onclick=\"bcv(1,7,11)\">Gen 7:11</ref></sup> (<b>feminine</b> <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('MT')\"><bdbheb><reflink>ᵑ0</reflink></bdbheb></lookup> <ref ref=\"Gen 38:24\" b=\"1\" cBegin=\"38\" vBegin=\"24\" cEnd=\"38\" vEnd=\"24\" onclick=\"bcv(1,38,24)\">Gen 38:24</ref> but <b>masculine</b> Sam <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Di')\">Di</lookup>) <highlightword>(newness), new moon, month</highlightword> (on formation compare Lg<sup>BN 144</sup>; on usage, names, etc., <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('M-A')\">Muss-Arn<sup>JBL 1892, 72 ff., 160 ff.</sup></lookup>) — <bdbheb>׳</bdbheb><bdbheb>ח</bdbheb> absolute <ref ref=\"Gen 7:11\" b=\"1\" cBegin=\"7\" vBegin=\"11\" cEnd=\"7\" vEnd=\"11\" onclick=\"bcv(1,7,11)\">Gen 7:11</ref> +; construct (rare) <ref ref=\"Gen 29:14\" b=\"1\" cBegin=\"29\" vBegin=\"14\" cEnd=\"29\" vEnd=\"14\" onclick=\"bcv(1,29,14)\">Gen 29:14</ref> +; suffix <bdbheb>ח